  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## <i class=\"fa-solid fa-sparkles\"></i> Start Here <i class=\"fa-solid fa-sparkles\"></i>\r\n\r\nWelcome to **Web Lab**! You'll be using this editor and an AI Tutor to build websites.\r\n\r\nIn this activity, your project already includes planning files and folders. For now, just look around.\r\n\r\nIn future levels, you will use those files and AI Tutor Chat to design and build a webpage, step by step. \r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. Look at the Files panel just to the right of this panel.\r\n2. Find these files and folders:\r\n   * `content_ideas` \r\n   * `wireframes`  \r\n   * `images`  \r\n   * `style.md`\r\n3. Open the folders to browse the files inside\r\n4. Open style.md and skim the design directions inside.\r\n5. Do not ask AI Tutor to build the webpage, yet. On the next level, you will use the AI Tutor to explore the plan.\r\n\r\n> **Tip:** Click **“Code**,**” “Preview**,**”** or **“Split View”** to change how much of the page you can see. On Chromebooks, press F11 to make your workspace larger!\r\n>\r\n> ![](https://images.code.org/886be386cc8082c8d6ab23938bd8cd26-image-1776373130068.png)\r\n\r\nOnce you have familiarized yourself with Web Lab click **Continue**.",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "true",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
